{"title":"2009 AIME II Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#The_&quot;obvious&quot;_substitution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The \"obvious\" substitution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/0/cb07e848f9188a9fd706d99ab6513a7d949c48a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"20\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/b/34b671ab48de5392b8ddbd64c268ab86395fa0f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec29c1234be5b7b72a98bd9dee9e11adda51e384.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n + 1} = \\frac85a_n + \\frac65\\sqrt {4^n - a_n^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"203\" height=\"37\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f0d43e758d9cef0fe802a89ff590f52ee8d766f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Find the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f659be762622558799a9119468b5008cb1b27f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span id=\"The_.22obvious.22_substitution\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_&quot;obvious&quot;_substitution\">The \"obvious\" substitution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: The &quot;obvious&quot; substitution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>An obvious way how to get the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c78734258d2d82aeb28c1631e8f1798154c888d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> from under the square root is to use the substitution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e66e1a853bd2703f362084ca95c097e3bf1be5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = 2^n b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />. Then the square root simplifies as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5637c675f961008aa8f0bff4fb164287b2798d24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{4^n - a_n^2} = \\sqrt{4^n - (2^n b_n)^2} = \\sqrt{4^n - 4^n b_n^2} = 2^n \\sqrt{1 - b_n^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"441\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>The new recurrence then becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/b/18b6b523413e7da3eea99cc80491857890718238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_0=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/900f8dfb7f11032c2cd7a945955da6fdc62d189f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{n+1} = \\frac45 b_n + \\frac 35\\sqrt{1 - b_n^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"189\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can now simply start to compute the values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" /> by hand:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a485e50f12da8c31ce9cc1c126b1dbb6d47cf453.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} b_1 &amp; = \\frac 35 \\\\ b_2 &amp; = \\frac 45\\cdot \\frac 35 + \\frac 35 \\sqrt{1 - \\left(\\frac 35\\right)^2} = \\frac{24}{25} \\\\ b_3 &amp; = \\frac 45\\cdot \\frac {24}{25} + \\frac 35 \\sqrt{1 - \\left(\\frac {24}{25}\\right)^2} = \\frac{96}{125} + \\frac 35\\cdot\\frac 7{25} = \\frac{117}{125} \\\\ b_4 &amp; = \\frac 45\\cdot \\frac {117}{125} + \\frac 35 \\sqrt{1 - \\left(\\frac {117}{125}\\right)^2} = \\frac{468}{625} + \\frac 35\\cdot\\frac {44}{125} = \\frac{600}{625} = \\frac{24}{25} \\end{align*}\" width=\"481\" height=\"219\" />\n</p><p>We now discovered that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df2deca051b6b36f14eb9d9ff55409408e696e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_4=b_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />. And as each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/15099c8a57653ee3bb64e4815c3165de59750f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> is uniquely determined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" />, the sequence becomes periodic. In other words, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/6517bbac3b34a2e1040d5cde292f36ec02865a5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_3=b_5=b_7=\\cdots=\\frac{117}{125}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"193\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/4395eb7180d7b5b5793724d377d1fdea00c80468.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2=b_4=\\cdots=b_{10}=\\cdots=\\frac{24}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"236\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore the answer is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/3/653bc8d8e87697fd661d1f9c8887df8b83781814.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\lfloor a_{10} \\rfloor &amp; = \\left\\lfloor 2^{10} b_{10} \\right\\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor \\dfrac{1024\\cdot 24}{25} \\right\\rfloor  = \\left\\lfloor \\dfrac{1025\\cdot 24}{25} - \\dfrac{24}{25} \\right\\rfloor  \\\\ &amp;  = \\left\\lfloor 41\\cdot 24 - \\dfrac{24}{25} \\right\\rfloor = 41\\cdot 24 - 1 = \\boxed{983} \\end{align*}\" width=\"396\" height=\"92\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>After we do the substitution, we can notice the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c762ce20934cd16663302d19f97c728a7be05730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( \\frac 35 \\right)^2 + \\left( \\frac 45 \\right)^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"148\" height=\"46\" />, which may suggest that the formula may have something to do with the unit circle. Also, the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00faaf039537d5f88afb5e07ba38a5d08f8c857c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{1-x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> often appears in trigonometry, for example in the relationship between the sine and the cosine. Both observations suggest that the formula may have a neat geometric interpretation.\n</p><p>Consider the equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed18b9372c799785fe24f29c8529be40f61e9768.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = \\frac45 x + \\frac 35\\sqrt{1 - x^2}\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Note that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f388fe7d19a4e766e76735e67529df89fa6a4f53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=\\sin^{-1} \\frac 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"85\" height=\"37\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/d/cbd6ec8d7401c72713bd5ff9e02b765afb1695cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin t=\\frac 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"67\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7c8d5f963b414227447a5311ecd5bd49d00191.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos t = \\frac 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"37\" />. Now suppose that we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a7ab078374eb9881bf5c64f2634179963fc7ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\sin s$\" width=\"68\" height=\"12\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Then our equation becomes:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/7/6170bc6dbf6d00f1d035a014f899f3164276b746.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=\\cos t \\cdot \\sin s + \\sin t \\cdot |\\cos s|\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Depending on the sign of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f1e914f7b225aad90858d2f1f3b3ded95055378.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos s$\" width=\"35\" height=\"8\" />, this is either the angle addition, or the angle subtraction formula for sine. In other words, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2ebdef37e5d5f1cd9f627acc72f6719a94d6b0f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos s \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec684734a0014e6525e24b1be02a87120b20747d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\sin(s+t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />, otherwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/2795fe4bb68cdbfd59137ddf7cf66534f774b1f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\sin(s-t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/0/d10dd007f4dad541a809a121a8fd302749748c7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_0=0=\\sin 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c2e2d12c8c69bc656ead238cab01c71d647d8bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 = \\sin(0+t) = \\sin t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"169\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913749fc6f4c4d5485ba993357a2d21903ab0090.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2 = \\sin(t+t) = \\sin (2t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" />, and so on. (Remember that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is the constant defined as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f388fe7d19a4e766e76735e67529df89fa6a4f53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=\\sin^{-1} \\frac 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"85\" height=\"37\" />.)\n</p><p>This process stops at the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/3/0538944e2ec826f2374e8efff25911f0e0ea36e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = \\sin (kt)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/0/c80b07c752b43df35d56b45b1215835459d48b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kt$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> exceeds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/0112fc17b564678a107e44298fa2526fafe9a761.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" />. Then we'll have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd23cafa07ba61c65799f17b860262f60a52b92b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+1} = \\sin(kt - t) = \\sin ((k-1)t) = b_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"317\" height=\"18\" /> and the sequence will start to oscillate.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbcb8ba713347abfb35e0ce0f55438287a08b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\frac{\\pi}6 = \\frac 12 &lt; \\frac 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"113\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80ee7fa709715bc1a054a27763e4cdd08f86d605.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\frac{\\pi}4 = \\frac{\\sqrt 2}2 &gt; \\frac 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"128\" height=\"41\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is strictly between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e5db1f1dbace53d2d4b15f91898d98018c16d7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/d/29d56fade5c97aac465df3da145efa77e85dd608.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/221711b9e54aa46a5217d79dd7440872e9a25a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2t\\in\\left(\\frac{\\pi}3,\\frac{\\pi}2 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"94\" height=\"33\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e70f74a28f48c5ff7362c34e66615c34a1685c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3t\\in\\left( \\frac{\\pi}2, \\frac{3\\pi}4 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"107\" height=\"43\" />. Therefore surely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3eaac3ed6f78a02995c46051481d7713684bbfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2t &lt; \\frac{\\pi}2 &lt; 3t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"94\" height=\"33\" />. \n</p><p>Hence the process stops with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20b72a664c73d94461bf5466cdf3b8524d3c1c69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_3 = \\sin (3t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, we then have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a37c0e7434192f4d90f9ddf908a4491ba2dd674a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_4 = \\sin (2t) = b_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" />. As in the previous solution, we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/5245258e4050e31a1da341ddf7dbe153f5875951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{10}=b_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, and that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/e/60e0cd01062fbb5abf8cc019269d9892aa3ee32e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor a_{10} \\rfloor  = \\left\\lfloor 2^{10} b_{10} \\right\\rfloor = \\boxed{983}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"189\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z5uZ2PGmIUg\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z5uZ2PGmIUg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II\" title=\"2009 AIME II\">2009 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2009 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2009\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2009 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2009 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2009 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2009 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2009 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_II_Problems/Prob